          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For camping, buy a compressor fridge, not a thermoelectric cooler. The Dometic CFX3 45 is the best overall and the most efficient on a battery; the ICECO VL45ProS gives you a SECOP compressor and a 5-year compressor warranty for less; the BougeRV CR45 is the right buy for most weekend campers on a budget. Choose the EcoFlow GLACIER Classic only if you need a built-in battery away from the vehicle.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then plan the power. A 45-liter fridge uses roughly 300 to 450Wh a day in summer, so a 1kWh power station covers a long weekend, and 100W to 200W of solar plus a battery keeps it running indefinitely. Get the battery protection setting right, run it from 12V rather than AC, and you will never buy a bag of ice again.
